## A clear glass pane, two parallel faces 0.1 apart, before a red matte backdrop. A blue matte
## panel beside the camera lies outside its frustum: it shows in the pane only as a reflection,
## so the red channel reads what the pane transmits and the blue channel what it reflects. Each
## light reaches one surface, from the side its viewer is on, and no shadow ray crosses the pane.
## Kd 0.01 keeps interreflection, which only the path tracer renders, below the tolerance the
## test measures; the lights make up the radiance. Not third-party.
Display "glassparams_pane.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 64 48 1
PixelSamples 2 2
Option "pathtracer" "integer samples" [512]
Projection "perspective" "fov" [40]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "distantlight" 1 "from" [0.8 0.5 -0.33] "to" [0 0 0] "intensity" [260]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "from" [0.8 0.5 0.33] "to" [0 0 0] "intensity" [500]
## begin backdrop
AttributeBegin
Surface "matte" "Kd" [0.01]
Color [1 0 0]
Polygon "P" [-12 -9 3  12 -9 3  12 9 3  -12 9 3]
AttributeEnd
## end backdrop
## begin panel
AttributeBegin
Surface "matte" "Kd" [0.01]
Color [0 0 1]
Polygon "P" [1.5 -3 -3  6 -3 -3  6 3 -3  1.5 3 -3]
AttributeEnd
## end panel
## begin pane
AttributeBegin
Surface "glass"
Polygon "P" [-2.7 2.1 0  2.7 2.1 0  2.7 -2.1 0  -2.7 -2.1 0]
Polygon "P" [-2.7 -2.1 0.1  2.7 -2.1 0.1  2.7 2.1 0.1  -2.7 2.1 0.1]
AttributeEnd
## end pane
WorldEnd
